{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-118581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(t),$ what is the carrying capacity of the following logistic growth model?\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=720y-8{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=8y(90-y),\\,y(0)=5.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=90.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $90.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "47d82ee7a93d18c924fc603304e9fa5f6a8f4baa04d8f7eb6d0b60c3e24462e5"} {"question" "q-118581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "720"] ["math" "80"] ["math" "90"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "90"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(t),$ what is the carrying capacity of the following logistic growth model?\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1\\,750y-7{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=20\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=7y(250-y),\\,y(0)=20.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=250.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $250.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "47d82ee7a93d18c924fc603304e9fa5f6a8f4baa04d8f7eb6d0b60c3e24462e5"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "250"] ["math" "500"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-118580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "250"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-119842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(t),$ what is the carrying capacity of the following logistic growth model?\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=1\\,350y-9{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=25\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-119842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=ky(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nA diagram showing a typical logistic growth curve is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/assets/57f4b604c546daed4f1cb3895191fae0ccac33b5c17aac705f203f0a837c7e69.png)\n\nFirst, let's factor the right-hand side of the given equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9y(150-y),\\,y(0)=25.\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that $a=150.$ Therefore, the carrying capacity is $150.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-119842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "47d82ee7a93d18c924fc603304e9fa5f6a8f4baa04d8f7eb6d0b60c3e24462e5"} {"question" "q-119842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7db60036502bb576f02b883fd885a93c3d25258f65013f5106a84183aa22e01"} {"question" "q-119842" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "150"] ["math" "1\\,350"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045108/state.json" "file_s